Third-party works
-----------------

The Chatterbox text-to-speech family
(crates/izwi-core/src/models/architectures/chatterbox) is a Rust port of:

* Chatterbox (https://github.com/resemble-ai/chatterbox)
  Copyright (c) 2025 Resemble AI. MIT License.
* PerTh, the watermarker Chatterbox applies to its audio
  (https://github.com/resemble-ai/Perth)
  Copyright (c) 2025 Resemble AI. MIT License.

and of the parts of these works that Chatterbox builds on:

* CosyVoice (https://github.com/FunAudioLLM/CosyVoice): the S3Gen flow
  decoder and the HiFT vocoder. Copyright (c) 2024 Alibaba Inc.
  Apache License, Version 2.0.
* WeNet (https://github.com/wenet-e2e/wenet) and ESPnet
  (https://github.com/espnet/espnet): the Conformer encoder.
  Copyright (c) 2019 Shigeki Karita; Copyright (c) 2020 Johns Hopkins
  University (Shinji Watanabe); Copyright (c) 2020-2021 Mobvoi Inc.
  Apache License, Version 2.0.
* S3Tokenizer (https://github.com/xingchensong/S3Tokenizer): the speech
  tokenizer used for voice cloning. Copyright (c) 2024 Tsinghua Univ.
  (Xingchen Song) and Dinghao Zhou. Apache License, Version 2.0.
  It is modified from Whisper (https://github.com/openai/whisper),
  Copyright (c) 2022 OpenAI, MIT License.
* Matcha-TTS (https://github.com/shivammehta25/Matcha-TTS): the flow
  decoder's U-Net and transformer blocks. Copyright (c) 2023 Shivam Mehta.
  MIT License.
* HiFi-GAN (https://github.com/jik876/hifi-gan): the vocoder's generator.
  Copyright (c) 2020 Jungil Kong. MIT License.
* Snake (https://github.com/EdwardDixon/snake): the vocoder's activation.
  Copyright (c) 2020 Edward Dixon. MIT License.
* CAM++ from 3D-Speaker (https://github.com/alibaba-damo-academy/3D-Speaker),
  as modified in FunASR (https://github.com/modelscope/FunASR): the speaker
  x-vector encoder. Copyright (c) FunASR. MIT License.
* Real-Time-Voice-Cloning (https://github.com/CorentinJ/Real-Time-Voice-Cloning):
  the voice encoder. Modified & original work Copyright (c) 2019 Corentin
  Jemine; original work Copyright (c) 2018 Rayhane Mama. MIT License.
* spacy-pkuseg (https://github.com/explosion/spacy-pkuseg), a fork of
  pkuseg-python (https://github.com/lancopku/pkuseg-python): the Chinese word
  segmenter of the multilingual text frontend. Copyright (c) 2020 ExplosionAI
  GmbH, 2018-2019 pkuseg authors. MIT License.

The Maya1 text-to-speech family
(crates/izwi-core/src/models/architectures/maya1) runs Maya Research's
Maya1 (https://huggingface.co/maya-research/maya1, Apache License,
Version 2.0) and includes a Rust port of the decoder of:

* SNAC (https://github.com/hubertsiuzdak/snac), the audio codec Maya1's
  tokens decode through. Copyright (c) 2023, Descript; Copyright (c) 2024,
  Hubert Siuzdak. MIT License.

The Maya 2 Native text-to-speech family
(crates/izwi-core/src/models/architectures/maya2) runs Maya Research's
Maya 2 Native (https://huggingface.co/maya-research/maya2-native, Apache
License, Version 2.0) and includes Rust ports of:

* Maya 2 Native's inference code (https://github.com/MayaResearch/maya2-native):
  the prompt layout, samplers, stop rule, loop guards and text normaliser.
  Copyright (c) 2026 Maya Research. Apache License, Version 2.0.
  Its normaliser's Assamese number words are AI4Bharat's indic-numtowords
  data (https://github.com/AI4Bharat/indic-numtowords, MIT License) and its
  Assamese month names come from the Unicode CLDR (Unicode License v3), both
  as Maya Research vendors them.
* SpeechBrain's ECAPA-TDNN speaker encoder and filterbank front end
  (https://github.com/speechbrain/speechbrain), whose
  spkrec-ecapa-voxceleb weights clone voices. Copyright (c) SpeechBrain
  contributors. Apache License, Version 2.0.

The shared Mimi codec (crates/izwi-core/src/models/shared/codecs/mimi) is a
Rust port of Hugging Face transformers' MimiModel
(https://github.com/huggingface/transformers, Copyright (c) Kyutai and The
HuggingFace Inc. team, Apache License, Version 2.0). It runs Kyutai's Mimi
weights (https://huggingface.co/kyutai/mimi), which Kyutai licenses under
Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 (CC BY 4.0,
https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/); izwi downloads them unmodified.

The LFM2.5 and LFM3 model families (crates/izwi-core/src/models/
architectures/lfm2, lfm25_audio, lfm3 and lfm3_audio), LFM3-Audio-2B
among them, run Liquid AI's open-weight checkpoints
(https://huggingface.co/LiquidAI), which izwi downloads unmodified. Liquid AI licenses them under the LFM Open License v1.0: use is
royalty-free, but commercial use by an entity with annual revenue of
US$10,000,000 or more is not licensed by it (see the LICENSE file in each
model repository). The LFM3 chat template and architecture were ported from
Liquid AI's model code, and the LFM3 GGUF layout from llama.cpp
(https://github.com/ggml-org/llama.cpp, MIT License). LFM3-Audio-2B's
speech encoder, MaskGIT depth decoder, LiquidCodec decoder and generation
loop were likewise ported from Liquid AI's model code.

